  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 8.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "okay, doctor, we're all set in here. I'll give you the numbers when you want them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.58,
      "end_seconds": 14.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.02,
      "end_seconds": 21.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a high reading at the pharmacy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 22.31,
      "end_seconds": 31.76,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "here are the numbers, doctor height 163 centimetres, temperature 36.7, weight 92 kilos, blood pressure 164 over 103, heart rate 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.38,
      "end_seconds": 34.16,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "okay noted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.2,
      "end_seconds": 47.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "When was the the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.49,
      "end_seconds": 59.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.92,
      "text": "uh, I'm not sure when it began, to be honest. Some weeks ago, but I can't say how many"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.11,
      "end_seconds": 64.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.83,
      "end_seconds": 85.39,
      "duration_seconds": 20.56,
      "text": "I'd call it mild. I've also had an occasional headache. With occasional headache, I'd give it a six, out of ten. Being a bit nervous at appointments was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.07,
      "end_seconds": 88.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "and what about breathlessness or visual changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.42,
      "end_seconds": 91.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "no, I'd have said so"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.12,
      "end_seconds": 95.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "any chest pain or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.27,
      "end_seconds": 99.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "none of those, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.32,
      "end_seconds": 109.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.98,
      "end_seconds": 113.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.37,
      "end_seconds": 118.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "right, are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.88,
      "end_seconds": 123.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Tamsulosin. I take it it at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.24,
      "end_seconds": 128.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Do you know the the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.34,
      "end_seconds": 142.82,
      "duration_seconds": 13.48,
      "text": "0.4 milligrams. Okay so it's atorvastatin 20 milligrams at night for my cholesterol. I take diclofenac 50 milligrams when needed for the joint pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 143.61,
      "end_seconds": 148.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 25 milligrams"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.62,
      "end_seconds": 154.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "okay have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.96,
      "end_seconds": 159.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.5,
      "end_seconds": 165.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "So, does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.9,
      "end_seconds": 174.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "my son has asthma my daughter has type 1 diabetes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.62,
      "end_seconds": 178.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.76,
      "end_seconds": 192.91,
      "duration_seconds": 8.15,
      "text": "An enlarged prostate for about ten years. High cholesterol for two years. I have arthritis in my knees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.54,
      "end_seconds": 197.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "a few questions about your lifestyle now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.25,
      "end_seconds": 208.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.36,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I look after my grandchildren most days. I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.16,
      "end_seconds": 214.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.79,
      "end_seconds": 225.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.9,
      "text": "Amoxicillin. I come out in... well, a rash all over. Nickel. I come out in... well, a rash on my skin"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.68,
      "end_seconds": 230.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.71,
      "end_seconds": 234.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Yeah, just my septum straightened, in my thirties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.53,
      "end_seconds": 241.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "let me look at the the area, I'll be gentle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.89,
      "end_seconds": 246.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "stay as you are for a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.44,
      "end_seconds": 260.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "your blood pressure is a little raised in the clinic but your heart sounds are normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.19,
      "end_seconds": 265.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.59,
      "end_seconds": 293.23,
      "duration_seconds": 9.64,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with possible white-coat blood pressure. I'd also keep early hypertension in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.9,
      "end_seconds": 297.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.82,
      "end_seconds": 307.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.41,
      "text": "I can't promise yet but most people with possible white-coat blood pressure do well once it's treated properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.71,
      "end_seconds": 345.2,
      "duration_seconds": 20.49,
      "text": "I'll request a 24-hour blood pressure monitor it'll help with raised clinic blood pressure. Cut back on salt and do a week of home readings. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit so we can settle the dose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.53,
      "end_seconds": 348.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Yes, will do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.39,
      "end_seconds": 354.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Book a review after the monitor. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.93,
      "end_seconds": 360.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "that's clear, thanks"
    }
  ]
}